0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 80 212 [
[(A simple way to build non-sinusoidal, periodic musical tones is to sum a)]
[(series of harmonically tuned sinusoids. Here the four oscillators have)]
[(frequencies in a 1:2:3:4 ratio \050the three [*] objects compute the second,)]
[(third, and fourth one\051. The amplitudes are adjusted by the [*~ 0.1], etc.,)]
[(objects. Note that, since the frequency \050from [mtof]\051 is a control)]
[(message, a [*] box suffices to operate on it, but the oscillator's output,)]
[(being an audio signal, needs [*~] instead. The control marked "overtones)]
[(ON/OFF" is a toggle switch. Click to turn it on and off. Of the overtones)]
[(are "off" you hear only a sinusoid from the first oscillator. If on, you)]
[(hear all four.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
